        "summary": "<p><strong><br /></strong></p>",
        "description": "<p>\n  <strong>Organizing university</strong>\n</p>\n<p>\n  University of Lagos<br />\n  <br />\n  <strong>Event description</strong>\n</p>\n<p>\n  The Entrepreneurship Development and Impact Program (EDIP) is a rigorous, intensive train-the-trainer initiative designed to transform selected Afretec Network faculty members into expert mentors capable of fostering a culture of innovation, entrepreneurship, and job creation across diverse academic disciplines.<br />\n  Through this programme, participating institutions will build lasting, in-house capacity to deliver high-quality entrepreneurship education long after the training concludes — creating a multiplier effect that extends across student populations, research communities, and the wider entrepreneurial ecosystem in each country represented.<br />\n  <br />\n  <strong>Participants</strong>\n</p>\n<p>\n  It is open to both Afretec members and other<strong><br /></strong>\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Pillar</strong>\n</p>\n<p>\n  Pathways to Opportunities\n</p>",
